  "units" [id="bp-node-units", label="Following the VIM4 2CD
principle (measurement
unit, 1.12: a "reference quantity with which any other quantity of the same kind can be compared by ratio") and Dybkær §13.3.3 (a unitary kind value is "a reference quantity multiplied by a number"), units are indexed by the kind they measure.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: Following the VIM4 2CD principle (measurement unit, 1.12: a "reference quantity with which any other quantity of the same kind can be compared by ratio") and Dybkær §13.3.3 (a unitary kind value is "a reference quantity multiplied by a number"), units are indexed by the kind they measure. (15 nodes)"];
  "extensivity" [id="bp-node-extensivity", label="Mass is extensive: the
mass of a whole is the sum
of the masses of its parts. Volume on mixing is not: ethanol and water mix sub-additively. Tracking which kinds are extensive is a precondition for soundly aggregating measurements.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: Mass is extensive: the mass of a whole is the sum of the masses of its parts. Volume on mixing is not: ethanol and water mix sub-additively. Tracking which kinds are extensive is a precondition for soundly aggregating measurements. (31 nodes)"];
  "spine_specialization" [id="bp-node-spine-005Fspecialization", label="Specializes relates kinds
to kinds. Flater (NIST TN
1943 §6.2) stresses the result is a lattice, not a tree. We generate it as the reflexive–transitive closure of an application-supplied direct-parent edge relation, so each "system of quantities" supplies its own hierarchy.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: Specializes relates kinds to kinds. Flater (NIST TN 1943 §6.2) stresses the result is a lattice, not a tree. We generate it as the reflexive–transitive closure of an application-supplied direct-parent edge relation, so each "system of quantities" supplies its own hierarchy. (4 nodes)"];
  "functions" [id="bp-node-functions", label="The algebraic calculus
rides on the toolchain
classes for multiplication, division, and reciprocal. There is no toolchain class for exp , sin , or square root, so the one genuinely new artifact is a carrier capability — the function-layer analogue of the numeric carrier — and a family of smart constructors that each carry their own metrological discipline. The functions split into five families with genuinely different kind signatures: kind-preserving ( abs , min , max ); powers and roots (the dimension scales by the exponent); dimensionless transcendentals ( exp , log — pure number in, pure number out); the trigonometric functions (a plane angle in, a number out — curated so that sin of a reflectivity stays a category error); and logarithmic levels (dB, neper — where log of a ratio demotes the scale, so the product calculus correctly refuses it).", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The algebraic calculus rides on the toolchain classes for multiplication, division, and reciprocal. There is no toolchain class for exp , sin , or square root, so the one genuinely new artifact is a carrier capability — the function-layer analogue of the numeric carrier — and a family of smart constructors that each carry their own metrological discipline. The functions split into five families with genuinely different kind signatures: kind-preserving ( abs , min , max ); powers and roots (the dimension scales by the exponent); dimensionless transcendentals ( exp , log — pure number in, pure number out); the trigonometric functions (a plane angle in, a number out — curated so that sin of a reflectivity stays a category error); and logarithmic levels (dB, neper — where log of a ratio demotes the scale, so the product calculus correctly refuses it). (5 nodes)"];
  "classification" [id="bp-node-classification", label="The canonical pattern is
the product , which covers
a large fraction of the ISQ (area = length · length, volume = area · length, energy = force · length). The general machinery lives in the Mathlib-free core; the dimensional refinement ( k.dim = k₁.dim · k₂.dim ) lives in the dimension layer, and analysis-shaped relations (area as a surface integral) in the Mathlib-backed layer.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The canonical pattern is the product , which covers a large fraction of the ISQ (area = length · length, volume = area · length, energy = force · length). The general machinery lives in the Mathlib-free core; the dimensional refinement ( k.dim = k₁.dim · k₂.dim ) lives in the dimension layer, and analysis-shaped relations (area as a surface integral) in the Mathlib-backed layer. (5 nodes)"];
  "iso80000_part3_classified" [id="bp-node-iso80000-005Fpart3-005Fclassified", label="The closed-form
certificate is the product
(a rectangle's area is width × height); the general certificate is the integral (an area is the area of an actual surface). Both classify the one area kind, and a property of the defining relation transports to every quantity certified under it.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The closed-form certificate is the product (a rectangle's area is width × height); the general certificate is the integral (an area is the area of an actual surface). Both classify the one area kind, and a property of the defining relation transports to every quantity certified under it. (2 nodes)"];
  "scale_spanning" [id="bp-node-scale-005Fspanning", label="The dimension layer can
detect some scale-spanning
units: a unit whose dimension is mechanically reducible — expressible in mass, length, and time alone — is by that fact not dimensionally independent. The candela (power) and the mole (one) are reducible this way. The kelvin is the sharp case: this work keeps thermodynamic temperature Θ as an independent dimension (the Thermodynamics chapter needs it), so the dimension layer sees the kelvin as if it were a base — its scale-spanning character is visible only once one adopts k_B as a defining coefficient, which the dimension layer does not. So scale-spanning is carried, like a kind's identity , above the dimension.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The dimension layer can detect some scale-spanning units: a unit whose dimension is mechanically reducible — expressible in mass, length, and time alone — is by that fact not dimensionally independent. The candela (power) and the mole (one) are reducible this way. The kelvin is the sharp case: this work keeps thermodynamic temperature Θ as an independent dimension (the Thermodynamics chapter needs it), so the dimension layer sees the kelvin as if it were a base — its scale-spanning character is visible only once one adopts k_B as a defining coefficient, which the dimension layer does not. So scale-spanning is carried, like a kind's identity , above the dimension. (7 nodes)"];
  "iso80000_part10_collision" [id="bp-node-iso80000-005Fpart10-005Fcollision", label="The dimension-collision
capstone, on standard
quantities: the dimension map identifies absorbed dose with dose equivalent, while the kind layer keeps them apart, both as kinds and as units (the gray and the sievert). The becquerel collision ( T⁻¹ ) is the companion.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The dimension-collision capstone, on standard quantities: the dimension map identifies absorbed dose with dose equivalent, while the kind layer keeps them apart, both as kinds and as units (the gray and the sievert). The becquerel collision ( T⁻¹ ) is the companion. (3 nodes)"];
  "iso80000_part12_collision" [id="bp-node-iso80000-005Fpart12-005Fcollision", label="The dimension-collision
capstones, on standard
quantities: the dimension map identifies the members of each family, while the kind layer keeps them apart, both as kinds and as units .", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The dimension-collision capstones, on standard quantities: the dimension map identifies the members of each family, while the kind layer keeps them apart, both as kinds and as units . (3 nodes)"];
  "iso80000_part13_units" [id="bp-node-iso80000-005Fpart13-005Funits", label="The dimension-one
collision capstone, on
standard quantities: the dimension map identifies information content, traffic intensity, and storage capacity, while the kind layer keeps them apart, both as kinds and as units (the shannon, the erlang, the bit).", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The dimension-one collision capstone, on standard quantities: the dimension map identifies information content, traffic intensity, and storage capacity, while the kind layer keeps them apart, both as kinds and as units (the shannon, the erlang, the bit). (3 nodes)"];
  "iso80000_part5_energy" [id="bp-node-iso80000-005Fpart5-005Fenergy", label="The energy species are
individuated by an
examination principle — here the potential's defining construction — and arranged as a specialization lattice over the general energy kind. The sharpest case is the Helmholtz versus the Gibbs energy: both "free energies" of the same dimension, they are nonetheless different kinds — and the calculus proves it from their differing natural variables, not from a naming convention.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The energy species are individuated by an examination principle — here the potential's defining construction — and arranged as a specialization lattice over the general energy kind. The sharpest case is the Helmholtz versus the Gibbs energy: both "free energies" of the same dimension, they are nonetheless different kinds — and the calculus proves it from their differing natural variables, not from a naming convention. (3 nodes)"];
  "metrological_modularity_mereology" [id="bp-node-metrological-005Fmodularity-005Fmereology", label="The fifth clause is
declared aggregation, and
it is the port-level form of the mereology chapter's vocabulary: a kind is extensive , intensive , whole-proper , or quasi-extensive , and a weighted carving carries the aggregation license. The clause puts that vocabulary on the boundary — each produced port declares its class — so the license to shard, tile, or stitch a module's batch axis is derived from the declarations rather than held as deployment convention. Requirement R27 states the obligation; the distribution license below is the theorem that discharges it.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The fifth clause is declared aggregation, and it is the port-level form of the mereology chapter's vocabulary: a kind is extensive , intensive , whole-proper , or quasi-extensive , and a weighted carving carries the aggregation license. The clause puts that vocabulary on the boundary — each produced port declares its class — so the license to shard, tile, or stitch a module's batch axis is derived from the declarations rather than held as deployment convention. Requirement R27 states the obligation; the distribution license below is the theorem that discharges it. (2 nodes)"];
  "iso80000_part4_force" [id="bp-node-iso80000-005Fpart4-005Fforce", label="The force species are
individuated by an
examination principle and arranged as a specialization lattice over the general force kind. The sharpest case is static versus kinetic friction: physically the same dimension and both "friction forces", they are nonetheless different kinds — and the calculus proves it from their differing measurement conditions, not from a naming convention.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The force species are individuated by an examination principle and arranged as a specialization lattice over the general force kind. The sharpest case is static versus kinetic friction: physically the same dimension and both "friction forces", they are nonetheless different kinds — and the calculus proves it from their differing measurement conditions, not from a naming convention. (3 nodes)"];
  "foundations_square" [id="bp-node-foundations-005Fsquare", label="The four corners of Lowe's
square, as the calculus
carries them: the system (substantial particular), its sort (substantial universal), the kind-of-property (non-substantial universal, from the spine), and the individual quantity (mode). The identity discipline Designated is what makes naming a corner a claim.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The four corners of Lowe's square, as the calculus carries them: the system (substantial particular), its sort (substantial universal), the kind-of-property (non-substantial universal, from the spine), and the individual quantity (mode). The identity discipline Designated is what makes naming a corner a claim. (4 nodes)"];
  "iso80000_part11_homonyms" [id="bp-node-iso80000-005Fpart11-005Fhomonyms", label="The homonym families are
individuated by the
examination principle alone — distinct_of_examPrinciple , not the id strings, which are equal. Every characteristic number has the same coherent unit symbol 1 , so the unit cannot tell them apart either; yet two are not commensurable, because they reference different kinds.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The homonym families are individuated by the examination principle alone — distinct_of_examPrinciple , not the id strings, which are equal. Every characteristic number has the same coherent unit symbol 1 , so the unit cannot tell them apart either; yet two are not commensurable, because they reference different kinds. (4 nodes)"];
  "trustmodel" [id="bp-node-trustmodel", label="The interaction algebra is
curated , and it pays to
be precise about what the type system guarantees for a curated edge: explicitness and propagation, not truth . Every kind-changing operation demands a witness naming the full kind equation at its call site, and no mechanism — no inference, no instance search, no coercion — can introduce an edge silently. But whether a written edge is metrologically right is the author's claim, exactly as an axiom is a claim a proof assistant checks everything against but never for . This section fixes the two poles the discipline sits between, and shows the residue between them is finite, local, and mechanically enumerable.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The interaction algebra is curated , and it pays to be precise about what the type system guarantees for a curated edge: explicitness and propagation, not truth . Every kind-changing operation demands a witness naming the full kind equation at its call site, and no mechanism — no inference, no instance search, no coercion — can introduce an edge silently. But whether a written edge is metrologically right is the author's claim, exactly as an axiom is a claim a proof assistant checks everything against but never for . This section fixes the two poles the discipline sits between, and shows the residue between them is finite, local, and mechanically enumerable. (2 nodes)"];
  "metrological_modularity" [id="bp-node-metrological-005Fmodularity", label="The interface clause and
the judgments on it. A
boundary is declared , so a membership choice can be wrong about it — and the two decidable comparisons below are exactly the two ways it can be wrong: not the boundary the members compute, or not a faithful deployment of the tier below.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The interface clause and the judgments on it. A boundary is declared , so a membership choice can be wrong about it — and the two decidable comparisons below are exactly the two ways it can be wrong: not the boundary the members compute, or not a faithful deployment of the tier below. (4 nodes)"];
  "iso80000_part5_scale" [id="bp-node-iso80000-005Fpart5-005Fscale", label="The kelvin and the degree
Celsius are both
well-formed metrological units — a kind bears a unit from the differential (interval) scale upward, not only from ratio scale, so the degree Celsius is a legitimate unit even though × , ÷ are undefined on Celsius temperatures. What separates the two kinds is the scale type : ratio versus interval.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The kelvin and the degree Celsius are both well-formed metrological units — a kind bears a unit from the differential (interval) scale upward, not only from ratio scale, so the degree Celsius is a legitimate unit even though × , ÷ are undefined on Celsius temperatures. What separates the two kinds is the scale type : ratio versus interval. (2 nodes)"];
  "iso80000_part3_length" [id="bp-node-iso80000-005Fpart3-005Flength", label="The length species are
individuated by an
examination principle and arranged as a specialization lattice over the general length kind. This is what lets the calculus answer the question the standard leaves to prose — why is a width not a distance? — with a proof rather than a naming convention, while keeping the two comparable so an explicit up-cast to length is still available.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The length species are individuated by an examination principle and arranged as a specialization lattice over the general length kind. This is what lets the calculus answer the question the standard leaves to prose — why is a width not a distance? — with a proof rather than a naming convention, while keeping the two comparable so an explicit up-cast to length is still available. (4 nodes)"];
  "iso80000_part3_area" [id="bp-node-iso80000-005Fpart3-005Farea", label="The metric tensor is
realized as the Gram
matrix of the two tangent vectors ∂r/∂u , ∂r/∂v (its entries are the classical E , F , G ); its determinant is g ; and the surface element is dA = √g . The standard writes the element with g ; the area-consistent Riemannian element is its square root , and the formalization makes that convention explicit by proving that a flat patch then recovers its Euclidean area. The kind whose magnitudes these areas are is the catalogued quantity -kind area, dimension L² .", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The metric tensor is realized as the Gram matrix of the two tangent vectors ∂r/∂u , ∂r/∂v (its entries are the classical E , F , G ); its determinant is g ; and the surface element is dA = √g . The standard writes the element with g ; the area-consistent Riemannian element is its square root , and the formalization makes that convention explicit by proving that a flat patch then recovers its Euclidean area. The kind whose magnitudes these areas are is the catalogued quantity -kind area, dimension L² . (5 nodes)"];
  "iso80000_part3_volume" [id="bp-node-iso80000-005Fpart3-005Fvolume", label="The metric tensor of a
region is the 3 × 3 Gram
matrix of its three tangent vectors; its determinant is g ; the volume element is dV = √g , and the volume is its integral. The kind is the catalogued quantity -kind volume, dimension L³ .", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The metric tensor of a region is the 3 × 3 Gram matrix of its three tangent vectors; its determinant is g ; the volume element is dV = √g , and the volume is its integral. The kind is the catalogued quantity -kind volume, dimension L³ . (2 nodes)"];
  "object_types" [id="bp-node-object-005Ftypes", label="The object of an
individual quantity (the
foundations chapter's mode) ranges over an arbitrary type. The gate needs nothing from it; the designation needs Designated , whose injectivity field is what distinguishes a designation from a formality.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The object of an individual quantity (the foundations chapter's mode) ranges over an arbitrary type. The gate needs nothing from it; the designation needs Designated , whose injectivity field is what distinguishes a designation from a formality. (8 nodes)"];
  "foundations_carving" [id="bp-node-foundations-005Fcarving", label="The particular-side
mereology as data: the
carving (a description of a whole into parts, one among many) and the part/whole roles a single portion-total pair carries.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The particular-side mereology as data: the carving (a description of a whole into parts, one among many) and the part/whole roles a single portion-total pair carries. (2 nodes)"];
  "iso80000_part6_power" [id="bp-node-iso80000-005Fpart6-005Fpower", label="The power species are
individuated by an
examination principle — here which component of the periodic process the quantity isolates — and arranged as a specialization lattice over the general power kind. The sharpest case is active versus reactive power: both "powers" of the same dimension, they are nonetheless different kinds — and the calculus proves it from their differing defining constructions, not from a naming convention, while the standard itself separates their units, W from var .", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The power species are individuated by an examination principle — here which component of the periodic process the quantity isolates — and arranged as a specialization lattice over the general power kind. The sharpest case is active versus reactive power: both "powers" of the same dimension, they are nonetheless different kinds — and the calculus proves it from their differing defining constructions, not from a naming convention, while the standard itself separates their units, W from var . (3 nodes)"];
  "iso80000_part3_prefix" [id="bp-node-iso80000-005Fpart3-005Fprefix", label="The prefix layer is added
beside the
metrological-unit layer, not inside it: a prefixed unit carries its provenance — which prefix, which base — and projects to an ordinary metrological unit of the same kind. So every fact already proved about units (commensurability, well-formedness) transfers to the projection unchanged, while the provenance lets the conversion factor and the multiple/submultiple distinction be read off rather than restated.", shape="tab", style="filled", fillcolor="#166534", color="#16a34a", penwidth="2.4", fontcolor="#f8fafc", peripheries=1, tooltip="Group View: The prefix layer is added beside the metrological-unit layer, not inside it: a prefixed unit carries its provenance — which prefix, which base — and projects to an ordinary metrological unit of the same kind. So every fact already proved about units (commensurability, well-formedness) transfers to the projection unchanged, while the provenance lets the conversion factor and the multiple/submultiple distinction be read off rather than restated. (2 nodes)"];
  "iso80000_part6_relations" [id="bp-node-iso80000-005Fpart6-005Frelations", label="The product , quotient ,
